{
  "sn22.7:0.1": "Linked Discourses 22.7 ",
  "sn22.7:0.2": "1. Nakula’s Father ",
  "sn22.7:0.3": "Anxiety Because of Grasping ",
  "sn22.7:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn22.7:1.2": "“Mendicants, I will teach you how grasping leads to anxiety, and how not grasping leads to freedom from anxiety. ",
  "sn22.7:1.3": "Listen and apply your mind well, I will speak.” ",
  "sn22.7:1.4": "“Yes, sir,” they replied. ",
  "sn22.7:1.5": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "sn22.7:2.1": "“And how does grasping lead to anxiety? ",
  "sn22.7:2.2": "It’s when an unlearned ordinary person has not seen the noble ones, and is neither skilled nor trained in the teaching of the noble ones. They’ve not seen true persons, and are neither skilled nor trained in the teaching of the true persons. ",
  "sn22.7:2.3": "They regard form as self, self as having form, form in self, or self in form. ",
  "sn22.7:2.4": "But that form of theirs decays and perishes, ",
  "sn22.7:2.5": "and consciousness latches on to the perishing of form. ",
  "sn22.7:2.6": "Anxieties occupy their mind, born of latching on to the perishing of form, and originating in accordance with natural principles. ",
  "sn22.7:2.7": "So they become frightened, worried, concerned, and anxious because of grasping. ",
  "sn22.7:3.1": "They regard feeling as self … ",
  "sn22.7:3.2": "",
  "sn22.7:3.3": "",
  "sn22.7:3.4": "",
  "sn22.7:3.5": "",
  "sn22.7:4.1": "They regard perception as self … ",
  "sn22.7:4.2": "They regard choices as self … ",
  "sn22.7:4.3":